{"name":"Dry Dock","hex":"#817665","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dry dock","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of drydock"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dry_dock"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dry dock","blocks":[{"text":"A dry dock is used for the construction, maintenance, and repair of ships, boats, and other watercraft.\nThere are several basic types of dry docks:"},{"items":["Graving or basin docks","Floating dry docks","Marine railways","Vertical lifts","Marine travel lifts"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/USS_Greeneville_%28SSN_772%29_-_dry_dock_Pearl_Harbor_%281%29.jpg/330px-USS_Greeneville_%28SSN_772%29_-_dry_dock_Pearl_Harbor_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dry_dock"},{"title":"Dock","blocks":[{"text":"The word dock in American English refers to one or a group of human-made structures that are involved in the handling of boats or ships. In British English, the term is not used the same way as in American English; it is used to mean the area of water that is next to or around a wharf or quay. The exact meaning varies among different variants of the English language."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Cruise_ship_dock_in_St_Maarten.JPG/330px-Cruise_ship_dock_in_St_Maarten.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dock"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Littoral_combat_ship_in_drydock%2C_San_Diego.jpg/500px-Littoral_combat_ship_in_drydock%2C_San_Diego.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Littoral_combat_ship_in_drydock%2C_San_Diego.jpg/1280px-Littoral_combat_ship_in_drydock%2C_San_Diego.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai